0.0630.09when the magnetization is tipped backup onto the longitudinal axis with a -90" pulse. Thus, T2 relaxation effects are imprinted into the longitudinal magnetization before imaging. In other words, after this procedure, the available longitudinal magnetization is scaled according to the T2 relaxation occurred during TEp. The FLASH readout block typically implements a center-out k-space trajectory ordering to encode the T2-prepared contrast in the first readouts close to the k-space center. The resulting image has a T2 weighting depending on TEp. A T2 map (i.e., a spatial representationSVG
