[0044]    At step 305, the MRI system creates a voxel-wise signal from the intensity values that are provided by the different reconstructed images for a same voxel. Preferentially, the intensity values are concatenated to obtain the voxel-wise signal. In other words, the MHI system is configured for collecting, in each reconstructed image, the intensity value that is associated to the voxel that represents the same position within the imaged part of the biological object (i.e. for each voxel of a reconstructed image, the intensity value associated to the concerned voxel in the reconstructed image and the intensity value associated to the same voxel in all other reconstructed images are collected and associated tosaid voxel, i.e. to a position within the imaged part).SVG
